  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Two Fully Read",
      "items": [
        "Claude Code: sessions, tokens, spend and the plan's real usage windows, priced end-to-end",
        "Codex CLI: sessions, tokens and rate limits counted exactly - shown unpriced rather than priced with an invented rate card"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Detected Is Not Read",
      "items": [
        "detected and hasData are separate facts the board refuses to conflate",
        "Windsurf is the live example: ~/.windsurf exists and holds zero bytes of usage",
        "Cursor, Gemini CLI, Copilot, Windsurf, Antigravity, Aider are listed as installed - never as an empty board that looks broken"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Devin: Activity, Not Usage",
      "items": [
        "Local session databases carry no cost and almost no token data, so reporting spend would mean inventing it",
        "The probe counts .db files and reads timestamps - it never opens one, and no SQLite engine ships in the agent",
        "Real accounting lives in Devin's cloud API behind a per-user key; calling it would break \"nothing leaves your machine\""
      ]
    }
  ]
